# Files excluded from the Vercel deployment. (Phase 3C-2)
#
# Vercel builds from the LOCAL FILESYSTEM, not from git, so .gitignore protects nothing
# here: an untracked or git-ignored file still ships unless it is listed below.
#
# Only two things need to be publicly served — latest.json and editions/** — plus the
# api/ directory, which Vercel compiles into functions. Everything else is internal.
# Images come from images.unsplash.com and audio from Cloudflare R2, so no media is
# served from Vercel and none can be broken by this file.

# ── credentials: never upload, under any circumstances ──────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*

# ── build and tool output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vercel/
.wrangler/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ── CI, tooling and internal scripts ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.github/
scripts/

# ── the Python pipeline: source, tests, fixtures and working files ──────────────────
pipeline/
*.py

# ── local experiments and historical material ───────────────────────────────────────
scratch/
archive/

# ── documentation ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
docs/
*.md

# ── build configuration that must not be published ──────────────────────────────────
# The local build confirmed both functions still compile with this excluded.
tsconfig.json

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   api/                 compiled into the /api/auth/exchange and /api/edition functions
#   api/_lib/            imported by those functions
#   api/_certs/          the vendored Apple root certificates, bundled and read at runtime
#   latest.json          the live feed manifest
#   editions/            the published editions
#   package.json,        required for dependency installation and function bundling
#   package-lock.json
